NAME
       lvrename - rename a logical volume

SYNOPSIS
       lvrename VG OLDNAME NEWNAME
       lvrename /dev/VG/OLDNAME /dev/VG/NEWNAME

DESCRIPTION
       lvrename gives a logical volume a new name inside its volume group.
       The data is not touched and a mounted LV keeps working, but its device
       paths change (/dev/VG/NEWNAME, /dev/mapper/VG-NEWNAME). Update
       /etc/fstab if it names the LV by path; entries that use the UUID keep
       working.

EXAMPLES
       Rename the LV data in vgdata to projects:

           lvrename vgdata data projects
           lvs vgdata

SEE ALSO
       vgrename(8), lvs(8), lvm(8)
